      "reason": "Hensel spectral idempotents commute with every A_j and recover the original possibly non-idempotent block condition. The graph Gram determinant is 1+4 epsilon_i mod8. Necessity uses the F2 residue field of each specified ring, not O/2 as a field. Pairing the odd diagonal positions followed by Gram–Schmidt gives a genuine base T when all epsilon vanish."
    },
    {
      "id": "column-norm-lifting",
      "classification": "valid",
      "reason": "Audited the full iterative lifting lemma including m=2: at stage m off-diagonal H+H^T kills the current symmetric error, free diagonal H kills next norm bits, and 2^(2m) is divisible by 2^(m+2). Projection to H_i preserves a given finite class. Thus the extra column norm mod2^(M+1) is necessary and sufficient, and the exact C/R counts and q^s/q^t fibers follow."
    },
