    },
    {
      "id": "sharp-descent",
      "classification": "valid",
      "reason": "For M≥3, rational-part polar normalization corrects by at least 2^(2M−3), giving M−1 descent; M=2 uses T. Vanishing theta coefficient mod2^M is necessary and sufficient for full precision. Rank-one block groups are {±1}, so all-rank-one gives exact descent. The stated Cayley witnesses have unit denominators even for M=2: 1+2i and 3, respectively, and their off-diagonal theta coefficients have valuation exactly M−1."
    },
    {
      "id": "arbitrary-finite-extension-supplement",
      "classification": "valid",
      "reason": "For B=O/2, Artin–Schreier has kernel {0,1}, is bijective on the nilradical, and its residue image is the zero absolute-trace space. The complete-graph trace-degree constraints have n−1 independent binary relations and each diagonal has exactly two choices. This proves G2=2 q^(n choose2); the same lifting lemma yields every higher count and the alternating-matrix kernel. No independent supplementary error found."
    }
